From: X-Wrt developers
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: retain flow ownership on PPE transaction failures

Treat failed SRAM reads as unknown, not expired. Propagate invalidation
errors without unlinking flow ownership, and retain ACNT0 until its reset
is acknowledged. Reserve natflow slots before requesting writes so even
an ambiguous ADD timeout can be rolled back without reusing live slots.

Keep failed natflow deletions in quarantine and retry them from delayed
work. Reject replacement while retirement fails and skip keepalives for
retiring records. Disable the AN7563 PPE under the retirement lock before
cancelling work and releasing quarantine at device teardown.

TC deletions also propagate invalidation errors. Publish their software
ownership before exposing entries to RX binding to avoid unowned flows
when software table insertion fails.

